<%# The shared template. One file answers a browser and a native client.

     turbo-frame needs no translation: it is spelled the same in Turbo HTML and
     in the protocol. `p` is an HTML element name that ApplicationController
     declares as an alias of the DemoText component, so the same element means
     a paragraph to a browser and a DemoText to a native client.

     Everything here is well-formed XML on purpose. `tag.br` and the other
     void-element helpers write `<br>`, which no XML parser will read, and
     form_with writes accept-charset, which the protocol does not admit on a
     form owner. Neither belongs in a shared template. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(@greeting, :frame) do %><p id="<%= dom_id(@greeting) %>">One template, two audiences</p><% end %>
